    "narrative": "Our strongest play for today is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (85.34), who benefits from an elite matchup against Drake (6.26 xERA). The combination of a porous opposing arm and a high-leverage #2 spot in the order cements him as our clear anchor. **Bryce Harper** (78.74) also stands out as a high-end start; he enjoys a massive park-factor boost (+16%) and favorable wind conditions, making him a prime candidate for a multi-hit game. Additionally, **Tyler Freeman** (67.75) offers excellent value in a deep slot, as the favorable matchup against Avila helps mitigate the typical drop-off associated with the #8 spot.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Gleyber Torres** (47.63), who fell just shy of our rotation. While he benefits from a park upgrade, he was squeezed out by the efficiency scores of our high-speed middle infielders, specifically **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Masyn Winn**, who provide critical utility in our quest to hunt stolen bases. We also continue to monitor **Yainer Diaz** (40.93); he is barely holding his spot above our floor and faces a major hurdle in the elite arm of deGrom (3.08 xERA). His score is dangerously low, and he remains our primary candidate to swap out should an alternative emerge.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding **Daulton Varsho** (44.45), whose value is significantly capped by a poor platoon matchup against the lefty Mathews. Despite the park boost, his efficiency is hovering near the \"marginal\" threshold, and we will be watching his early-game at-bats closely. **Will Smith** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving our catching depth thin. As always, keep an eye on our reserves like **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Dylan Beavers**, who remain ready to cycle into the rotation if weather or late-scratch lineups shift the expected efficiency of our current starters.",
